.TH ICED\-LIBADWAITA\-NUMBER\-INPUT 3 "" "iced-libadwaita 0.1.0" "iced-libadwaita Manual"
.SH NAME
number_input \- an entry for a number with handles that step it (Mantine's NumberInput)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
NumberInput::new(text: &'a str, on_input: impl Fn(String) \-> M + 'a)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBNumberInput\fR: an entry for a number with handles that step it (Mantine's \fBNumberInput\fR).
.PP
The number is a fixed\-point \fBDecimal\fR, never a float: \fBdecimals\fR is how many fraction digits it keeps (0 is an integer), \fBmin\fR / \fBmax\fR bound it and \fBstep\fR is what a handle adds or takes. The rules are the \fBnumeric\fR primitive.
.PP
The app keeps only the text (so typing is not interrupted), and the widget has one message: \fBon_input(text)\fR, for typing and for a handle (which sends the stepped number formatted with the digits). Read the number with \fBNumeric::parse\fR. Text that is not a number or is out of range draws the error state.
.PP
.nf
.RS
NumberInput::new(&self.text, Msg::Text)
    .decimals(2)
    .min(0)
    .max(100)
    .step(Decimal::new(25, 2))   // 0.25
.RE
.fi
.PP
The handles are two small buttons stacked in the right section, dimmed at a limit; \fBhandles(false)\fR hides them. Arrow keys and the wheel are not included: iced has no focus model to hang them on.
